        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the west‑flowing Pequea Creek, part of the Susquehanna River watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Paradise features a covered bridge and an old mill, classic landmarks that echo the region’s Amish heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://paradisetownship.org/welcome-to-paradise/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cherry Crest Adventure Farm offers rides, a petting zoo, and seasonal produce stands, drawing families to Amish Country’s heart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://paradisetownship.org/welcome-to-paradise/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1994, Paradise was the filming location for the comedy “Trapped in Paradise,” giving the town a moment in Hollywood history.",
